  "issue_number": 3470,
  "issue_title": "Add a weight-setters leaderboard (by validator) to /leaderboards",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\nThe issue's current body says: \"GET /api/v1/chain/weights/setters \u2014 a validator-level weight-setting leaderboard, twin of the route above\" (the \"twin\" is #3469's `/api/v1/chain/weights`). That backend route is real and live \u2014 `handleChainWeightSetters` in `workers/request-handlers/analytics.mjs:1361` and `loadChainWeightSetters`/`buildChainWeightSetters` in `src/chain-weight-setters.mjs` \u2014 but nothing in `apps/ui` calls it: no query function in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts`, no component, no route. Separately, **`/leaderboards` is not a route that exists** \u2014 `apps/ui/src/routes/` has no `leaderboards.tsx`; the only thing called \"leaderboards\" today is `LeaderboardsModule` (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx`), a fixed five-board *subnet-ranking* module (healthiest/fastest-rpc/most-complete/most-enriched/fastest-growing, driven by `leaderboardsQuery()` \u2192 `/api/v1/registry/leaderboards`) mounted on the homepage (`apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx:178`). It has nothing to do with validator weight-setting activity, so this issue's title destination is aspirational, not an existing anchor to extend.\n\n## Requirement\n\nRender the network-wide weight-setter leaderboard \u2014 the individual validators driving consensus across every subnet, ranked by their total `WeightsSet` count over a 7d/30d window \u2014 as a new ranked table on the `/explorer` page, the nearest existing home for a network-wide, chain-direct leaderboard (this issue's own sibling cluster, e.g. #3467/#3468, targets \"the explorer page\" for the same class of network-wide leaderboard; a dedicated `/leaderboards` route does not exist and is out of scope here).\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/weights/setters` (optional `?window=7d|30d`, default `7d`; `?limit=` default 20, max 100; `?format=csv` also supported)\n- Query function: **none exists.** Searched `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` for any `chainWeightSetters`/`ChainWeightSetters` reference \u2014 zero hits. The only weight-setters query present is the per-subnet twin, `subnetWeightSettersQuery` (queries.ts:2972-2986), which calls `/api/v1/subnets/${netuid}/weights/setters` and normalizes into a `SubnetWeightSetters` shape (`normalizeSubnetWeightSetters`, queries.ts:2952). This PR must add the network-wide equivalent \u2014 a `chainWeightSettersQuery(window)` following the same `queryOptions` + `apiFetch` + `normalize*` pattern used by dozens of sibling queries in that file (e.g. `chainSignersQuery` at queries.ts:2347, or `subnetWeightSettersQuery` itself) \u2014 **as well as** the UI wiring, both in one PR. A data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n  - Response shape to normalize (from `buildChainWeightSetters`, `src/chain-weight-setters.mjs:85-116`): `{ schema_version, window, observed_at, distinct_setters, weight_sets, setter_count, setters: [{ hotkey, uid, weight_sets, share, first_set_at, last_set_at }] }`. `hotkey` is nullable (a uid-only setter has no network-wide identity), `share` is nullable when the network total is zero.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` \u2014 add a `ChainWeightSetters` / `ChainWeightSetter` type pair mirroring the existing `SubnetWeightSetters`/`SubnetWeightSetter` types (same file already has that pair; find it and match its shape exactly, adding `netuid`-free fields since this is network-wide).\n- `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` \u2014 add `chainWeightSettersQuery(window: ChainWindow = \"7d\")`, placed near the other `chain*` queries (e.g. beside `chainSignersQuery` at queries.ts:2347), following its `queryOptions`/`apiFetch`/`normalize` structure.\n- `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` \u2014 extend `ExplorerDashboard()` (starts at line 225) with a new ranked-table section, added to the two-column grid that already holds \"Top fee payers\" (the `<div className=\"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2\">` block starting around line 353, whose second `<section>` is the \"Top fee payers\" table at ~line 397-444). Add the fetch alongside the existing `useSuspenseQuery(chainSignersQuery(win))` call (line 233) and add `\"/api/v1/chain/weights/setters\"` to the `<ApiSourceFooter paths={[...]}>` list (line 78-83).\n- Exact anchor to copy: the \"Top fee payers\" `<table>` (explorer.tsx ~397-444) \u2014 same `TH` header class (line 89), same `<Link to=\"/accounts/$ss58\" params={{ ss58: ... }}>` + `shortHash(...)` identity cell pattern (line 425-431), same `hover:bg-surface/40` row style and empty-state `<p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">` paragraph.\n- What to render: a \"Network weight-setters\" table with columns Validator (hotkey, linked to `/accounts/$ss58` via `shortHash`, falling back to `uid` when `hotkey` is null \u2014 do not link a uid-only row to an account page), WeightsSet count (`weight_sets`, `formatNumber`), Share (`share` as a percentage, `\u2014` when null), Last set (`last_set_at`, relative time if a `<TimeAgo>`-style helper already exists in the codebase, else the raw ISO). Section header shows `{distinct_setters}` validators, matching the \"Top fee payers\" header's `{fees.top_fee_payers.length} accounts` convention.\n- Coordination note: **#3469** (\"Add a network-wide weight-setting activity chart to /leaderboards\") targets the sibling route `/api/v1/chain/weights` and also has no existing query function or UI wiring \u2014 both issues will likely touch `explorer.tsx` and `queries.ts` in the same area. Land in either order, but whichever merges second should rebase past the first rather than re-deriving the same `ChainWindow`/`chainSignersQuery`-adjacent scaffolding.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` (`explorer.tsx`) in addition to `queries.ts`/`types.ts`\n- [ ] `explorer.tsx` imports and calls the new `chainWeightSettersQuery` via `useSuspenseQuery` (matching the existing `chainActivityQuery`/`chainFeesQuery`/`chainCallsQuery`/`chainSignersQuery` calls already in `ExplorerDashboard()`)\n- [ ] The rendered table shows, per row: validator identity (hotkey linked to the account page, or uid fallback when hotkey is null), `weight_sets` count, `share`, and `last_set_at`\n- [ ] The section header reports `distinct_setters` and respects the page's existing `7d`/`30d` window toggle (`Route.useSearch().window`)\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states match the file's existing convention: `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary` at the page level (already wired in `ExplorerPage`, lines 72-76) and an inline `{list.length > 0 ? <table>\u2026 : <p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">No \u2026 yet.</p>}` branch for the empty case, mirroring the \"Top fee payers\" section\n- [ ] `/api/v1/chain/weights/setters` is added to the `ApiSourceFooter` paths list in `explorer.tsx`\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Building a dedicated `/leaderboards` route \u2014 that does not exist today and is not this issue's scope.\n- Implementing #3469's network-wide weight-setting *activity chart* (the aggregate/intensity view) \u2014 this issue is the setter-level leaderboard only.\n- Touching `LeaderboardsModule` (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx`) or its homepage mount \u2014 that module's five subnet-ranking boards are unrelated to validator weight-setting.\n- Per-subnet weight-setters UI \u2014 `subnetWeightSettersQuery` already exists; whether it's wired into the subnet page is tracked separately (see #3480, \"Add a weight-setters leaderboard to the subnet validators panel\").\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
